# Database changes

- Inspect the actual installed schema state. An unmerged branch may already have migrations installed in an application database.
- For installed migrations, add a forward migration and preserve data. Test the changed upgrade path with representative old records and a fresh install when relevant.
- Run destructive rebuilds only against an explicitly disposable isolated database. Verify its connection before the command.
- Application data removal requires Omar's explicit authorization for that action and database.
- Use exact money types, documented constraints, deliberate indexes, and the project's MySQL/MariaDB semantics.
- Consider partial migration failure, backfill retry, and existing null or legacy values. Document any deployment write pause needed.
- Keep seeders targeted and safe to rerun. Respect rollback guards and append-only records.
